# Backend Performance

## Purpose

Avoid scalability footguns in server-side code.

## Database

- Eliminate N+1 queries — profile before shipping list endpoints.
- Pagination required for list APIs (cursor or offset — follow project standard).
- Connection pooling — reuse pool; never open connection per request ad hoc.
- Index consciously on filter/sort columns; verify with EXPLAIN on slow queries.

## Caching

- Cache read-heavy, slow-changing data (Redis, in-memory) with TTL.
- Invalidate on write — document cache key strategy.
- Never cache user-specific auth data in shared cache without key scoping.

## Concurrency

- Offload CPU-heavy work to background jobs.
- Use async I/O; avoid blocking event loop (Node) or thread pool exhaustion.
- Batch external API calls when possible.

## API Design for Performance

- Support field selection/sparse responses if GraphQL or `?fields=` is project pattern.
- Stream large exports instead of loading into memory.

## When to Flag

If proposing synchronous processing of large files, unbounded queries, or missing pagination — warn user and suggest alternative.